  {
    "type": 0,
    "content": "Now the other way is to sell it. BUT! Do NOT sell it to the trading post. As I hope I've informed all of you, the TP takes a 15% tax on all items sold, paid by the seller. But, the VALUE of that gear is defined by the TP, so why should you get 85% of the value of your loot? Enter the magic of Peer-to-peer trading, or trust-based mail trading. A TP baron (me) will pay 95% of the TP value for that gear, and profit 5% for our time spent processing.",
